<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Trastámara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1369">1369</a>–<a href="/years/1555">1555</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Trastámara was a Spanish royal dynasty named after the county of Trastámara in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. It came to the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in 1369, when Henry II killed his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile">Peter the Cruel</a>, and to the Crown of Aragon in 1412 through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compromise-of-caspe">Compromise of Caspe</a>. The marriage of Isabella I and Ferdinand II joined the two crowns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-trastamara.jpg" alt="House of Trastámara" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Queen_Isabella_of_Castile_(1492-1504).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
